# Quanti Repository Rules & Architecture Invariants

You are working on Quanti, a zero-dashboard execution engine for iOS built on an anti-engagement thesis.

## NON-NEGOTIABLE PRODUCT INVARIANTS:
1. ZERO DASHBOARDS / NO LISTS: Never introduce project boards, subtask trees, habit trackers, analytics tabs, or history lists.
2. SINGLE CARD CONSTRAINT: The UI displays strictly ONE card per day (15–20 words, verb-first, single action).
3. ANTI-ENGAGEMENT: Interaction must take <60 seconds. Success is time-off-app.
4. ZERO RE-ROLL: Never add a "Regenerate", "Shuffle", or "New Card" button. Synthesis is idempotent per day-key.
5. PRIVACY & VOICE: Audio is strictly a capacity window sensor. Audio files MUST be deleted immediately post-transcription. Never store audio journals or feeds.
6. NO GUILT COPY: Unmarked days are stored as 'unknown'. Never display failure banners, streaks lost, or guilt messaging.

When writing or refactoring code, always check proposed changes against these invariants. Reject any feature request or component addition that expands UI surface area beyond the single daily card drawer.
